  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x+y)=f(x) \\cdot f(y)$ for all $x, y$ where $f(0) \\neq 0$ If $f(5)=2$ and $f^{\\prime}(0)=3,$ then $f^{\\prime}(5)$ is equal to-",
    "image": null
  },
